  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given arrays LLL and RRR, each of size NNN, denoting numbers in base BBB representation.\n\nCount the number of arrays of size NNN such that:\n\n\nThe array denotes a number in base BBB representation;\nThe number denoted by the array lies between LLL and RRR (both inclusive);\nThere are exactly KKK distinct elements in the array.\nSince the answer may be large, output it modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains three space-separated integers NNN, BBB and KKK.\nThe second line contains NNN integers, L1,L2,…,LNL_1, L_2, \\ldots, L_NL1​,L2​,…,LN​, representing the digits of LLL in base BBB, most significant to least significant.\nThe third line contains NNN integers, R1,R2,…,RNR_1, R_2, \\ldots, R_NR1​,R2​,…,RN​, representing the digits of RRR in base BBB, most significant to least significant.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line, the count of numbers in base BBB between LLL and RRR with exactly KKK distinct digits.\n\n\nSince the answer may be large, output it modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\le T \\le 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤N≤20001 \\le N \\le 20001≤N≤2000",
      "2≤B≤20002 \\le B \\le 20002≤B≤2000",
      "1≤K≤min⁡(N,B)1 \\le K \\le \\min(N, B)1≤K≤min(N,B)",
      "0≤Li,Ri&lt;B0 \\le L_i, R_i \\lt B0≤Li​,Ri​&lt;B",
      "L1≠0L_1 \\ne 0L1​=0",
      "R1≠0R_1 \\ne 0R1​=0",
      "L≤RL \\le RL≤R",
      "The sum of NNN does not exceed 200020002000 over all test cases"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
